{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03OF", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:66a42082049353d0c1a524cf7955419332f9ebe03777a9f2cf21b1c64e5bbf88", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe can apply the descent of modules to study quasi-coherent sheaves.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e58ee94fd2f46c04abeae756c0a50edd7413102ee0956f3cd4adf3de471dba8e", "unit_id": "tag:03OF:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proposition", "parent_tag": "03OF", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\mathcal{F}^a : & \\Sch/S & \\to & \\textit{Ab}\\\\\n& (f: T \\to S) & \\mapsto & \\Gamma(T, f^*\\mathcal{F})\n\\end{matrix}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proposition}\n\\label{proposition-quasi-coherent-sheaf-fpqc}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proposition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:742b91af9464e7ed0137838e230d746a44319c9aca982b66f9ddee4a7ff6bafd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b6bc475d30b84b373641ce9a4e8ec09f138702f28bb9e4c9286134754c2b790e", "source_text": "For any quasi-coherent sheaf <MATH_0001> on <MATH_0002> the presheaf\n<MATH_0003>\nis an <MATH_0004>-module which satisfies the sheaf condition for the\nfpqc topology.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:32042c835970d531dfb101d85ea63e01ab55803f04d2e8b520a8b38887a448de", "unit_id": "tag:03OG:statement"}
